               "opportunityCheck":  "Mostly reasonable. The position score fits: process control was US$3.75B of US$4.14B quarterly revenue and the CEO calls it critical to the AI buildout. I would nudge AI revenue exposure up to about 12, because leading-edge logic, HBM and advanced packaging are now the main growth drivers behind the US$4.7B guide. Market growth looks fair given management\u0027s view of 2027 wafer-fab equipment spending above US$200B, but the November rout shows that growth is cyclical and rate-sensitive, so I would not raise it.",
               "technical":  "Trend is bearish. The 126.87 close sits below the EMA50 (164.20), EMA100 (174.53) and EMA200 (171.14); EMAs are smoothed average prices. The EMA50 has slipped under both longer averages, the classic sign that the medium-term trend has turned down. MACD (a trend-momentum gauge) is -8.26 vs a signal of -7.55 with a histogram of -0.71, so downside momentum re-accelerated on 20 Nov instead of fading. RSI 14 (a 0–100 momentum gauge; under 30 is oversold) is 32.74, near oversold but not there. Price closed below the lower Bollinger Band (129.90; middle 149.56), which signals a stretched move, though in heavy selloffs price can keep \u0027walking the band\u0027 lower. The stock is about 18% above the 52-week low of 107.20 and 59% below the 52-week high of 307.37. Volume of 22.6M vs a 15.0M 20-day average confirms real selling, and the close was near the day\u0027s low of 125.72. Support: 125.72, then 107.20. Resistance: 129.90, then about 139 (20 Nov open/high), then 149.56.",
               "fundamental":  "KLA sells the quality-control layer of chipmaking: inspection and metrology tools that every new node, HBM stack and advanced package needs more of. Fiscal Q1 2027 (quarter to 30 Sep, reported 28 Oct) brought record revenue of US$4.14B, up 13% q/q and 29% y/y, with non-GAAP EPS of US$1.22, above guidance. Semiconductor Process Control was US$3.75B. December-quarter guidance is US$4.7B ±0.2B with non-GAAP EPS of US$1.44 ±0.11 and non-GAAP gross margin around 62.5%. Management expects sequential growth for several quarters and 2027 wafer-fab equipment spending above US$200B. Capital returns were US$1.24B in the quarter. Nothing in November changed this picture, and Applied Materials\u0027 12 Nov guidance above consensus supports it.",
